# Normalise line endings in the repository, and pin the ones that break things.
#
# Shell scripts and the container entrypoint run on Linux. A CRLF copy fails
# there with `bad interpreter` or `$'\r': command not found` -- inside a Docker
# build that surfaces as a container which exits immediately with no useful
# message. Deciding this here rather than leaving it to each clone's
# core.autocrlf means a Windows contributor cannot commit a broken script.
#
# Go files are pinned for a smaller but equally concrete reason: gofmt writes LF
# and reports a CRLF file as unformatted, so a Windows checkout would fail any
# formatting check on files nobody touched.
* text=auto

*.sh        text eol=lf
*.go        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.svg text
